export anchor SheetMusicStyle:
    number: 95
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Sheet music
    idea: The dashboard engraved as a page of a printed score, with five line staves under the numbers, projects as numbered movements with tempo markings, and the fortnight's tasks as notes on a staff.
    base: light
    palette:
        manuscript: #fbfaf5, the score page and the style sheet
        desk: #e9e6dc, the backdrop around the page
        engraverBlack: #141414, notes, text, bar lines and the primary button
        staffGrey: #8a867c, the five staff lines, never text
        pencil: #4a463e, meta lines, captions and small numbers
        markingRed: #7d1d2c, dynamics, numbers over notes, rehearsal bars, Behind and overdue
        forest: #1e4d2b, On track
        umber: #7a4a00, At risk
        vellum: #efece2, the focus wash
    type:
        One serif family, Palatino Linotype, Book Antiqua, Palatino, Georgia,
        serif. The brand is 64px bold small caps, the greeting 42px italic,
        summary numbers 60px at 900 like a time signature, section heads
        24px bold small caps, movement names 24px italic, markings 15 to 22px
        bold italic, body 16px at 1.55 and captions 13 to 15px italic.
    layout:
        A thin top line holds the underlined search, the bell with a count
        and New project. The page is a white score sheet with wide margins on
        a grey desk. Its title block centres the brand in small caps over a
        subtitle, with Allegro moderato at top left and the date and the
        user as credits at left and right. The nav is a ruled row of links,
        each with a boxed rehearsal letter A to F, the current one filled
        black. The greeting is italic with a red sfz before the overdue
        line. The four numbers sit on one staff split into four measures by
        bar lines, each number set over five staff lines with its label
        below. Projects are six movements numbered I to VI, each row with
        the italic name and meta, a mini staff of ten note heads filled for
        each tenth done, the percent, and a tempo marking with the status.
        Below, the chart on a staff sits beside Programme notes, numbered by
        measure. Rows fold to two lines below 960px and the chart scrolls
        inside its box on phones.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 14px rows, 48 to 64px between sections and 72px page margins.
    density: Sparse. One project per line with lots of white between staves.
    corners: Square. The only curves are note heads and the fermata.
    borders: Hairline staff lines in fives, thin bar lines between measures, a thin and thick double bar to close a section, 1px ink rules under headings.
    shadows: None, apart from a 1px edge under the score page.
    icons:
        Engraving glyphs drawn in SVG. A stemmed note for On track with a
        tempo, a fermata for At risk with poco rit., and a hanging rest
        block for Behind with rall. Each status also shows its word.
    focus: A 2px black outline offset 3px with a vellum wash behind the control.
    tone: Concert programme Italian beside plain English, such as a tempo On track, The movements and Programme notes.
